            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-07-28T03:41:37+09:30" end-time-local="2026-07-28T03:41:37+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-07-27T18:11:37Z" end-time-utc="2026-07-27T18:11:37Z">
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A trough will continue to move over southeastern parts of the state today. A cold front will clip the far southeast this afternoon and evening before a high pressure system moves over the Bight from Wednesday. The high will extend a ridge across the state, as it slowly moves east into NSW by Saturday.</text>
                <text type="preamble">Wind and wave forecasts are averages. Wind gusts can be 40 per cent stronger than the forecast, and stronger still in squalls and thunderstorms. Maximum waves can be twice the forecast height.</text>
